WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:13.013
[rock music playing]

00:44.295 --> 00:51.302
CHAPTER 46:
EVEN IF I HAVE TO DROP OUT

00:54.805 --> 00:56.640
[slurps] Mmm.

00:59.810 --> 01:01.896
[sighs] What time does it start?

01:03.439 --> 01:05.483
Was it 9:00 am?

01:06.233 --> 01:09.445
Insane. A disciplinary committee?

01:09.528 --> 01:11.739
[sucks teeth] Just eat your food.

01:14.617 --> 01:16.035
Your novel became a big hit.

01:16.118 --> 01:17.453
So, what's the problem?

01:17.536 --> 01:18.829
Keep writing and make money.

01:19.371 --> 01:22.041
That way you can give me
a lot of pocket money.

01:22.958 --> 01:25.294
You can just drop out and take the GED.

01:31.717 --> 01:33.135
Your dad and I

01:33.219 --> 01:35.721
won't take your side
because we're your parents.

01:35.805 --> 01:40.059
We will accept whatever the school
decides to do about you. You understand?

01:40.935 --> 01:42.019
Honey…

01:48.442 --> 01:50.361
[sighs]

02:00.538 --> 02:01.914
What's the plan today?

02:04.625 --> 02:06.794
Shouldn't we come up with a plan together
or something?

02:08.212 --> 02:09.296
[sighs]

02:09.380 --> 02:11.298
Whatever you guys decide.

02:11.382 --> 02:12.383
That's right.

02:14.969 --> 02:17.555
I believe Eui-ju must
learn a lesson from this.

02:18.055 --> 02:19.849
Especially if she intends to keep writing.

02:21.016 --> 02:23.143
And eventually
make a living out of it too.

02:27.106 --> 02:30.568
[downcast music playing]

02:30.651 --> 02:33.320
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

02:36.782 --> 02:38.826
EPISODE 15

02:46.083 --> 02:47.626
Oh. [stammers]

02:57.011 --> 02:58.387
DISCIPLINARY COMMITTEE

03:12.443 --> 03:13.444
#GRADE HEAD - MS. JANG

03:13.527 --> 03:14.570
#HEAD OF STUDENT AFFAIRS
MR. SONG

03:14.653 --> 03:15.654
#VICE PRINCIPAL - MR. SEO

03:15.738 --> 03:16.780
I've asked you all here today,

03:16.864 --> 03:20.075
regarding Yeo Eui-ju and the novel
that she has written

03:20.159 --> 03:23.329
about her own teachers,
which you must've read by now.

03:23.412 --> 03:27.124
As you know the characters in the novel
are based on actual people, her teachers.

03:27.207 --> 03:29.001
And this raises concerns

03:29.084 --> 03:32.504
about the violation of
teachers' rights and defamation.

03:33.297 --> 03:36.216
Thus, I'd like your opinions
on how we should proceed with this.

03:36.967 --> 03:37.968
Ms. Kim,

03:38.552 --> 03:41.639
I was so shaken by it
that I couldn't even finish reading it.

03:42.222 --> 03:45.684
Oh… [chuckling]
…it was just too embarrassing.

03:45.768 --> 03:49.271
[clears throat] A mistake like this
can be made out of curiosity.

03:49.813 --> 03:52.900
And yet, she's at the stage
where her sexual identity

03:52.983 --> 03:56.445
as well as her own values must take root.

03:56.528 --> 03:59.782
I believe adults must stop her
from taking the wrong path.

03:59.865 --> 04:01.951
-[tense music playing]
-Since she is still a minor,

04:02.034 --> 04:03.869
she must be disciplined severely

04:04.453 --> 04:06.288
before she turns into a criminal.

04:06.372 --> 04:07.831
A crim…

04:08.582 --> 04:10.376
-A criminal?
-[clears throat]

04:10.459 --> 04:14.004
Ma'am, what are your thoughts then,
regarding the novel written by Eui-ju?

04:15.547 --> 04:16.757
Uh… [clears throat]

04:16.840 --> 04:21.136
Well… [sighs] …let me share a word
about this whole thing with you.

04:21.762 --> 04:25.099
First of all, I would like to apologize
if our daughter

04:25.182 --> 04:28.519
has caused discomfort and concern
to any of you here today.

04:29.228 --> 04:31.522
I only have myself to blame.

04:32.564 --> 04:35.776
It's… It's really all just my fault.

04:36.443 --> 04:39.947
I should've…
I should've paid more attention to her.

04:43.367 --> 04:45.202
However! [breathes shakily]

04:47.871 --> 04:52.626
How can a parent stop their child
from doing what they love?

04:55.295 --> 04:58.674
Especially when their child
shares with them…

04:58.757 --> 05:00.009
[sincere music playing]

05:00.092 --> 05:04.680
…that it's the… [sighs] …the only thing
that keeps them going in life.

05:05.889 --> 05:08.684
She's still too young
to have a good sense of judgment.

05:08.767 --> 05:10.686
Please give her a chance to reflect.

05:11.311 --> 05:13.814
-Please understand.
-[stammers] Please understand.

05:17.401 --> 05:18.861
Uh… [sighs]

05:18.944 --> 05:22.406
And now, let's hear from
the actual victims, the teachers.

05:22.489 --> 05:25.951
[smacks lips, sucks teeth] First of all,

05:26.827 --> 05:30.289
I'd like to say a word
on all of our behalf.

05:32.291 --> 05:34.752
Finding out the teachers
were dragged into this,

05:35.461 --> 05:37.212
I found that very shocking.

05:38.505 --> 05:42.885
Mmm, and then it hit me, "Is this what
they think every time they see me?"

05:42.968 --> 05:44.928
That feeling was really hard to shake.

05:47.806 --> 05:50.642
We've given this situation
some serious thought,

05:51.310 --> 05:53.937
therefore, we've come to a conclusion.

05:59.526 --> 06:00.611
[inhales sharply]

06:01.779 --> 06:03.572
What do you suggest we do, Ms. Kim?

06:04.448 --> 06:06.575
[owl hooting plays]

06:06.658 --> 06:10.204
[stammers] Whatever you decide,
we're all on board ma'am.

06:11.663 --> 06:14.124
Oh. [chuckles]

06:14.208 --> 06:18.253
Uh, what about the others? [chuckles]

06:18.337 --> 06:20.547
I want Eui-ju to take this chance

06:20.631 --> 06:23.801
to understand how serious it is
to write a novel about actual people,

06:23.884 --> 06:25.552
especially without their consent.

06:25.636 --> 06:27.554
It doesn't matter
if they're turned into fiction.

06:28.138 --> 06:30.349
And also she must not take it lightly.

06:32.726 --> 06:34.144
[sighs]

06:34.228 --> 06:35.854
Kill 'em with kindness, I guess.

06:36.772 --> 06:38.315
[inhales deeply]

06:39.525 --> 06:40.526
I'll…

06:41.485 --> 06:42.986
choose kindness.

06:45.072 --> 06:46.448
[Seo] That's ridiculous!

06:47.574 --> 06:50.994
If we let her slide like this,
it will destroy our school's authority.

06:51.078 --> 06:52.496
She must be expelled.

06:53.163 --> 06:54.998
Ma'am, let's expel her.

06:55.082 --> 06:57.417
[dramatic music playing]

07:02.923 --> 07:04.091
I told her to.

07:09.972 --> 07:11.849
I knew and I told her to keep writing it.

07:12.391 --> 07:14.143
It's my responsibility.

07:23.110 --> 07:26.321
Of course, when I first found out
I told her to delete it right away.

07:26.989 --> 07:28.407
I couldn't understand her.

07:29.074 --> 07:32.828
But Eui-ju knew what her dream was
and she was working to get closer to it.

07:32.911 --> 07:34.079
Her certainty…

07:36.498 --> 07:37.749
was very admirable.

07:41.461 --> 07:42.462
[groans]

07:43.172 --> 07:45.215
So, I just told her to keep going.

07:45.299 --> 07:47.467
To be there, to cheer for her,

07:48.677 --> 07:49.845
and to watch her grow.

07:54.558 --> 07:55.809
Eui-ju's a student

07:57.060 --> 07:59.980
who does get it done
once she puts her mind to something.

08:01.565 --> 08:02.900
Watching her as her homeroom teacher,

08:02.983 --> 08:05.569
I had no choice
but to respect her persistence.

08:06.528 --> 08:08.989
Now that we know her dream
is to be a writer,

08:09.072 --> 08:10.490
I'd give her a chance,

08:10.574 --> 08:15.329
so that her persistence…
can grow into real talent,

08:15.412 --> 08:19.458
and her energy and passion
can carry her all the way to her dream.

08:21.919 --> 08:22.920
Please understand.

08:32.930 --> 08:34.389
[inhales deeply]

08:34.473 --> 08:37.517
Let's hear from you too.
What do you say, Eui-ju?

08:38.310 --> 08:39.728
Are you going to keep writing?

08:39.811 --> 08:40.854
No, right?

08:44.066 --> 08:45.067
I…

08:45.567 --> 08:46.568
Yes?

08:53.283 --> 08:54.284
I…

08:55.077 --> 08:56.078
[inhales shakily]

08:59.331 --> 09:02.251
[inhales shakily]
I do want to keep writing.

09:03.168 --> 09:04.294
[stammers] What?

09:04.836 --> 09:08.090
[Eui-ju breathing shakily]
I'll accept any kind of punishment…

09:08.173 --> 09:09.174
[hopeful music playing]

09:09.258 --> 09:14.096
…and from now on, I'll write on my own,
only with my own ideas.

09:14.888 --> 09:18.767
And honestly,
I'm truly sorry for everything that I did.

09:19.434 --> 09:21.478
I've already deleted We Were Friends.

09:23.605 --> 09:25.315
But for me writing is…

09:28.402 --> 09:30.362
something I want to continue doing.

09:32.572 --> 09:34.366
Even if I have to drop out of school…

09:36.702 --> 09:38.245
I will keep writing novels.

09:47.838 --> 09:48.839
[groans]

09:49.464 --> 09:50.757
[sighs]

09:53.135 --> 09:55.470
I'll discuss this
with the teachers in charge first.

09:55.554 --> 09:56.555
And…

09:57.973 --> 10:01.143
in four days I'll let you know
what the punishment is. Let's go.

10:07.482 --> 10:08.900
-[sighs]
-My apologies.

10:09.484 --> 10:10.527
Goodbye.

10:11.028 --> 10:12.404
[Seo] Geez.

10:14.364 --> 10:15.365
[door closes]

10:16.366 --> 10:18.118
-I'm really sorry.
-[Da-ju] It's okay.

10:20.329 --> 10:25.584
Mr. Ga, I actually didn't know you were
her homeroom teacher all this time.

10:25.667 --> 10:26.710
It's all good.

10:27.502 --> 10:29.463
I should've been paying closer attention.

10:30.589 --> 10:33.175
-Please don't worry about it and go home.
-I see.

10:33.258 --> 10:34.593
Goodbye.

10:34.676 --> 10:36.470
I'll go speak with the principal.

10:36.553 --> 10:37.554
-Okay.
-Okay.

10:42.684 --> 10:44.019
[Ma, softly] Oh… Goodbye.

10:49.107 --> 10:51.985
Mom, Dad, you can… [stammers] …leave.

10:52.569 --> 10:53.653
Leave?

10:54.780 --> 10:55.781
Oh, okay.

10:55.864 --> 10:57.908
We'll… get going.

10:57.991 --> 10:59.743
See you at home.

10:59.826 --> 11:01.745
-[chuckles] Goodbye.
-Take care.

11:02.704 --> 11:03.705
Good luck in class.

11:07.292 --> 11:08.460
Eui-ju, back to class.

11:08.543 --> 11:10.921
We'll have to wait
for Mr. Ga to come back.

11:16.718 --> 11:18.136
I apologize for what I did.

11:19.930 --> 11:21.306
[both chuckle]

11:23.225 --> 11:25.227
I didn't expect to be
in your practice novel.

11:25.977 --> 11:28.146
I'm so sorry, Mr. Yoon.

11:28.230 --> 11:29.481
[sincere music playing]

11:29.564 --> 11:33.151
A writer writes stories based on
what they observe and imagine,

11:33.235 --> 11:36.488
but you must be careful
when it involves actual people.

11:37.072 --> 11:38.073
You understand that, Eui-ju?

11:39.199 --> 11:40.200
Yes.

11:40.700 --> 11:42.035
You know what?

11:42.119 --> 11:44.704
I saw this coming
when she wrote that reflection letter.

11:44.788 --> 11:48.250
Seriously, it had way more details
than it needed to have.

11:48.333 --> 11:52.379
So now I'm going to watch
how you do the Japanese essay homework.

11:53.255 --> 11:55.590
And if it doesn't touch my heart
in any way,

11:55.674 --> 11:57.175
I'll give you a flat-out F.

11:57.717 --> 11:58.718
-Yes.
-[chuckles]

11:58.802 --> 12:00.262
Poor Eui-ju. I mean…

12:00.846 --> 12:02.556
Mr. Jung, sorry. Because of me--

12:02.639 --> 12:03.974
Oh, no. Don't worry.

12:04.057 --> 12:05.392
I don't know much about writing anyway.

12:05.475 --> 12:07.018
[chuckles]

12:07.102 --> 12:09.729
But I hear you're quite good at it.

12:10.856 --> 12:11.857
Huh?

12:11.940 --> 12:12.941
That's what matters.

12:14.359 --> 12:16.945
Don't worry about it, Eui-Ju.
Just go back to class.

12:18.822 --> 12:20.157
Yes.

12:26.663 --> 12:28.081
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

12:28.748 --> 12:32.169
No matter how I look at this,
this is straight up defamation.

12:32.252 --> 12:34.963
[scoffs] I just cannot let this go.

12:35.046 --> 12:39.050
I-I-I'm getting a lawyer
and I'm taking this all the way.

12:39.134 --> 12:42.095
Don't worry it's just a joke, he's joking.
Go on. Go.

12:42.179 --> 12:45.098
I mean, why am I described
as someone so cheap, huh?

12:45.682 --> 12:46.683
Tell me,

12:47.225 --> 12:50.353
do you take me for someone who hides
instead of fighting for justice?

12:50.437 --> 12:52.731
-You don't fight for justice.
-Not at all.

12:52.814 --> 12:54.024
No. It's not true, right?

12:54.107 --> 12:55.650
[comical music playing]

12:55.734 --> 12:58.278
Hey, what if people actually see me
as that kind of person?

12:58.361 --> 13:00.280
-[Gi-jeon] That's what you're like.
-No way.

13:00.363 --> 13:02.699
-You did a good job.
-You did good. Really.

13:02.782 --> 13:04.034
His character, it was the best.

13:04.117 --> 13:06.161
[chuckles] Don't listen to him.

13:06.244 --> 13:07.871
-Go on, Eui-ju. Go, go.
-[Dong-ju] You did well.

13:07.954 --> 13:10.165
Hey! You have to change it!

13:10.248 --> 13:11.666
Oh, come on!

13:16.254 --> 13:17.255
-How did it go?
-Eui-ju.

13:17.339 --> 13:18.507
Oh, Eui-ju.

13:18.590 --> 13:19.966
-How did it go?
-What did they say?

13:20.050 --> 13:22.385
-What did they say? Come on, tell us.
-Uh…

13:22.469 --> 13:24.638
-What's the verdict?
-I'm not sure yet.

13:24.721 --> 13:26.056
They'll let me know after the meeting.

13:26.139 --> 13:27.349
-Oh, no.
-What?

13:27.432 --> 13:30.018
Then, will the results
come out today or when?

13:30.101 --> 13:31.353
What did they say?

13:31.436 --> 13:33.021
[Go-ya] And Mr. Ga, what did he say?

13:33.104 --> 13:35.398
Didn't he say anything? Come on, tell us.

13:36.024 --> 13:37.067
Actually,

13:37.943 --> 13:42.197
Mr. Ga already knew
because he's the one who caught me first.

13:42.280 --> 13:44.741
-Huh? He already knew?
-[chattering]

13:44.824 --> 13:47.244
-Mr. Ga?
-He said it was actually his fault

13:47.327 --> 13:51.498
because he's the one let me keep writing,
even after finding out about it.

13:51.581 --> 13:52.832
[Go-ya] He said that?

13:52.916 --> 13:55.919
[students gasping, whispering]

13:56.002 --> 13:58.255
[Dan-ji] So he actually
knew about the whole thing?

13:58.338 --> 14:01.091
Then…Then, what's going to happen now?

14:01.174 --> 14:03.009
[Eui-ju] I think
they're discussing it right now.

14:03.093 --> 14:04.636
[solemn music playing]

14:04.719 --> 14:07.722
Her novel's just as popular
as those by established writers.

14:08.515 --> 14:12.727
In terms of books, you can say it became
a bestseller as soon as it was published.

14:13.436 --> 14:15.564
So what if it's that popular?

14:15.647 --> 14:17.983
It's downright embarrassing. [huffs]

14:18.483 --> 14:20.819
There was a novel by a writer
named Love Hani

14:20.902 --> 14:22.654
when web novels first started.

14:22.737 --> 14:24.489
It was harshly criticized at first,

14:24.573 --> 14:27.742
but then it became popular enough
to be made into a film.

14:28.326 --> 14:32.080
Love Hani donated part of her royalties
to her alma mater.

14:32.789 --> 14:34.708
Could you imagine
how proud that school was?

14:34.791 --> 14:36.835
She donated her royalties?

14:39.671 --> 14:41.506
It's still no… Unacceptable.

14:41.590 --> 14:43.466
What are you staring at, Mr. Song?

14:44.134 --> 14:46.845
[inhales sharply] Can you please tell me
what you are reading?

14:47.512 --> 14:49.598
Oh, gosh, Ms. Kim.

14:49.681 --> 14:50.807
This is actually a big deal.

14:50.890 --> 14:52.142
See?

14:52.225 --> 14:54.436
I guess Eui-ju's novel is really popular.

14:54.519 --> 14:56.605
I mean, people are writing tons
of comments online.

14:57.188 --> 14:59.149
They all want to know why
she decided to leave

14:59.232 --> 15:00.775
and why she decided to delete the novel.

15:00.859 --> 15:02.569
Right, as if. [scoffs]

15:03.486 --> 15:04.654
How many could there be?

15:04.738 --> 15:06.865
How many read it?
Like a thousand? [chuckles]

15:06.948 --> 15:09.909
[chuckles] What?
What are you talking about? Huh?

15:09.993 --> 15:14.748
The most recent comments alone
add up to 108,420!

15:14.831 --> 15:17.083
What? That many people read it?

15:17.167 --> 15:19.461
[amusing music playing]

15:19.544 --> 15:21.713
Still, it's unacceptable.

15:21.796 --> 15:23.590
A student using her teachers
for a novel like that.

15:23.673 --> 15:25.717
Oh, wow. [chuckles]

15:25.800 --> 15:26.801
Guess what?

15:26.885 --> 15:29.137
They even started a petition
under the Committee

15:29.220 --> 15:31.848
-so they can get Imuk to come back.
-Mr. Song!

15:34.476 --> 15:37.729
My biggest concern is that
our school's reputation might be damaged

15:37.812 --> 15:39.481
if this information gets out.

15:39.981 --> 15:41.524
I see it differently.

15:41.608 --> 15:44.736
If anything, this shows that
our school produced a student

15:44.819 --> 15:46.488
with actual literary talent!

15:47.072 --> 15:48.114
Mr. Song, please.

15:50.784 --> 15:51.868
[clears throat]

15:51.951 --> 15:53.578
This is something to be grateful for.

15:55.747 --> 15:58.083
She could become sensational
like what's-her-name.

15:58.166 --> 16:01.920
The one who wrote Harry Potter.
I mean, it's possible, right? Hmm?

16:02.504 --> 16:04.756
-Right. Sure.
-That's right, Ms. Kim.

16:05.840 --> 16:08.677
Let's see now. [breathes deeply]

16:08.760 --> 16:10.679
[groans] What should we do?

16:11.471 --> 16:13.723
[groans]

16:15.767 --> 16:19.104
4 DAYS LATER

16:20.522 --> 16:21.981
[inhales sharply]

16:22.065 --> 16:27.278
Yeo Eui-ju's actions not only constituted
a serious violation of school rules,

16:27.362 --> 16:31.533
but they also had a negative impact
on all her fellow students.

16:35.453 --> 16:38.164
[inhales sharply]
However, given her genuine remorse

16:38.248 --> 16:41.543
and our belief that
she is fully capable of doing better

16:41.626 --> 16:44.295
we have decided to give her
one last chance.

16:44.921 --> 16:46.423
We will hold her accountable,

16:46.923 --> 16:49.509
but won't prevent her from her dreams.

16:50.218 --> 16:51.553
[inhales sharply]

16:51.636 --> 16:55.473
Therefore, Murim Girls' High School's
final decision in this matter will be…

16:55.557 --> 16:57.851
[dramatic music playing]

17:05.775 --> 17:07.444
…suspension for five days.

17:10.572 --> 17:13.908
[amusing music playing]

17:18.997 --> 17:19.998
Anyway…

17:20.498 --> 17:21.958
Am I in the novel?

17:24.169 --> 17:26.212
-What did they say?
-How did it go? Huh?

17:26.838 --> 17:27.881
I'm suspended…

17:29.048 --> 17:30.091
for five days.

17:31.176 --> 17:32.218
-Suspended?
-You're suspended?

17:32.302 --> 17:34.596
-Suspended!
-You're only suspended?

17:34.679 --> 17:36.931
[squealing, cheering]

17:37.015 --> 17:39.184
[triumphant, cheerful music playing]

17:39.267 --> 17:42.270
Hold up, should we celebrate
she's only getting suspended?

17:43.021 --> 17:44.939
What about college applications?

17:45.023 --> 17:48.526
Even with a perfect portfolio,
her record still matters.

17:48.610 --> 17:50.236
-Oh…
-No, no, no.

17:50.987 --> 17:54.073
I remember nothing stays on your record
unless it's a school violence issue.

17:54.157 --> 17:56.034
-Oh, really? Thank goodness.
-In any case,

17:56.117 --> 17:58.411
I'll have to accept it,
it's my fault after all.

17:58.495 --> 18:03.082
Oh, come on, what could be the problem
when it's just a suspension?

18:03.166 --> 18:05.168
[squealing, cheering]

18:08.505 --> 18:09.672
Let's go, let's go, let's go.

18:09.756 --> 18:11.007
[clamoring]

18:12.258 --> 18:15.136
CHAPTER 47:
BECAUSE YOU'RE MY FIRST STUDENT

18:15.970 --> 18:17.889
[class] Hello.

18:26.815 --> 18:28.441
I'm sure you've already heard

18:29.317 --> 18:30.568
that Eui-ju got suspended.

18:35.448 --> 18:38.117
It's only right for her
to take responsibility,

18:38.201 --> 18:41.246
but… I'm responsible as well.

18:42.580 --> 18:44.916
A teacher must always remain neutral,

18:45.542 --> 18:46.709
but I didn't.

18:46.793 --> 18:48.503
[sincere music playing]

18:49.546 --> 18:53.508
If this has hurt anyone's feelings,
I apologize.

18:56.010 --> 18:58.596
I'll try to pay more attention
to what you say,

18:58.680 --> 19:01.850
but I'll also ask you
to try to understand each other

19:01.933 --> 19:04.018
instead of arguing about
who did what wrong.

19:04.602 --> 19:05.812
[class] Yes, sir.

19:07.188 --> 19:08.982
Okay. Good luck with your classes today.

19:09.566 --> 19:11.192
Hey, sorry.

19:12.026 --> 19:13.027
Sorry.

19:13.111 --> 19:14.112
[door opens]

19:15.154 --> 19:16.281
[door closes]

19:16.364 --> 19:17.365
Thanks.

19:36.593 --> 19:37.594
What is it?

19:38.469 --> 19:41.514
I didn't get to thank you
for what you did for me.

19:42.265 --> 19:43.516
Thank you, Mr. Ga.

19:45.101 --> 19:46.311
Don't mention it, all right?

19:47.896 --> 19:49.480
So… [inhales sharply]

19:49.564 --> 19:53.067
…Mr. Ga, why would you
do something like that?

19:54.110 --> 19:55.320
Like what?

19:55.820 --> 19:59.657
You actually convinced the principal
and all the teachers.

19:59.741 --> 20:02.869
And I was just wondering why you did it.

20:08.708 --> 20:11.461
["Why This Night" playing]

20:18.676 --> 20:19.719
To me, you're…

20:29.395 --> 20:30.396
You are…

20:38.446 --> 20:39.656
my first student.

20:47.580 --> 20:48.665
Because…

20:50.083 --> 20:51.459
I'm just your student?

20:55.088 --> 20:56.923
Choi Ji-a, Eun Ha-su, and you,

20:57.465 --> 21:00.134
to me, are who actually deserve
some kindness.

21:03.471 --> 21:05.807
Stay away from trouble
while you're suspended.

21:05.890 --> 21:07.141
Go home.

21:29.163 --> 21:31.499
[whining]

21:31.582 --> 21:33.334
CHAPTER 48:
TURN OVER A NEW LEAF

21:33.418 --> 21:35.211
[funky, upbeat music playing]

21:36.045 --> 21:37.797
What? You can't have this.

21:37.880 --> 21:40.341
[Mom] Suni, go wake your sister up.

21:40.425 --> 21:42.552
[chuckles] Okay. All right.

21:48.683 --> 21:50.226
-Bang. [giggles]
-[Suni whines]

21:58.609 --> 21:59.610
[sighs]

22:05.158 --> 22:06.159
YEO EUI-JU

22:07.493 --> 22:09.037
[Da-ju] Mmm. Goodness.

22:15.710 --> 22:17.295
I'm gonna give it a try.

22:21.924 --> 22:26.429
I've finally decided to stop running away
before I see things through.

22:29.974 --> 22:32.685
-What's this about?
-Who are you talking about?

22:33.728 --> 22:36.147
[pensive music playing]

22:37.982 --> 22:40.610
-Going somewhere?
-[Da-ju] What is it?

22:43.154 --> 22:45.073
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

22:45.948 --> 22:48.242
-[chuckling]
-What is this?

22:48.326 --> 22:50.411
-I know it's supposed to be tofu…
-What is it?

22:50.495 --> 22:51.746
-…but this will do.
-Oh.

22:52.371 --> 22:54.248
-That's true.
-Hey!

22:54.332 --> 22:56.459
-It's not like she came back from prison.
-Ooh.

22:56.542 --> 22:57.794
-Sort of similar.
-I know.

22:57.877 --> 22:59.629
We can say she's been discharged.

22:59.712 --> 23:01.172
Now go live your life right, buddy!

23:01.255 --> 23:03.633
Mmm. Thanks so much, buddy.

23:03.716 --> 23:05.134
[students chuckling]

23:05.218 --> 23:06.552
-[chuckles]
-This is for you.

23:06.636 --> 23:07.887
Have this as you write.

23:07.970 --> 23:09.972
Don't let your sugar levels get too low.

23:10.890 --> 23:11.933
Thank you so much.

23:12.016 --> 23:14.560
-It's chocolate!
-Hey, don't mention it.

23:14.644 --> 23:17.772
Ooh! I have a GOAT writer friend!

23:17.855 --> 23:18.856
Listen.

23:19.440 --> 23:21.192
-Go, Eui-ju!
-Go, Eui-ju!

23:21.275 --> 23:23.194
-Let's go!
-Yeah!

23:23.277 --> 23:24.946
[Jenny] Try some! Try some!

23:25.029 --> 23:26.197
[Eui-ju] Okay, okay.

23:26.280 --> 23:28.199
-Eat something white to start your life.
-I'll give it a try.

23:28.282 --> 23:31.327
[cheering] Yes! Yeah!

23:33.955 --> 23:36.082
[cheering, chuckling]

23:36.165 --> 23:37.375
Have some! Have some!

23:37.458 --> 23:39.794
-Give me one!
-Hey! Only one!

23:47.718 --> 23:48.886
You know…

23:49.720 --> 23:52.765
I hated that you were getting
all Mr. Ga's attention.

23:56.185 --> 24:00.148
I felt like maybe
he would pay more attention to me

24:00.231 --> 24:01.399
if I ruined you.

24:03.484 --> 24:04.944
But I was wrong about it.

24:07.822 --> 24:09.407
I'm not gonna make excuses.

24:10.825 --> 24:12.535
I just want to apologize to you.

24:13.995 --> 24:15.121
I'm really sorry.

24:16.164 --> 24:18.499
[sincere music playing]

24:21.836 --> 24:23.087
[sighs]

24:24.297 --> 24:27.884
Thanks to you
I was able to own up to my mistakes.

24:28.843 --> 24:30.428
If none of this had happened,

24:30.511 --> 24:32.930
I would've kept writing
with all that guilt hanging over me.

24:39.020 --> 24:40.188
[chuckles]

24:42.231 --> 24:43.399
Let's get to the auditorium.

24:43.983 --> 24:46.402
The auditorium?
What about the morning assembly?

24:46.485 --> 24:49.113
We have Professor Na Deul-i's
lecture today.

24:49.197 --> 24:52.241
By the way,
she's not Mr. Ga's girlfriend, is she?

24:52.325 --> 24:54.827
One, two. Testing mic, testing.
Check, one, two.

24:54.911 --> 24:56.787
-Say ho, ho, ho!
-[crowd] Ho, ho, ho!

24:56.871 --> 24:57.872
[phone buzzes]

24:59.040 --> 25:02.919
Dan-ji wants me to bring her
a remote control from the media room.

25:03.002 --> 25:05.087
-Go on without me. [chuckles]
-Okay.

25:20.311 --> 25:21.479
Hello.

25:22.104 --> 25:23.147
Oh, hello there.

25:23.814 --> 25:27.318
Oh! Aren't you the student
from the coffee shop the other day?

25:28.277 --> 25:30.947
[sighs] It's so good
to see a familiar face.

25:31.906 --> 25:34.492
[chuckling]
I was feeling nervous, you see.

25:34.575 --> 25:35.576
Why?

25:36.619 --> 25:40.414
Well, I've hardly ever talked to
students before in my life.

25:41.249 --> 25:43.459
I hear students these days are scary.

25:43.542 --> 25:45.127
I'm worried I might make a mistake.

25:47.088 --> 25:48.422
The girls aren't mean.

25:49.006 --> 25:50.841
They won't bite you
unless you take their food.

25:50.925 --> 25:53.386
-[chuckling]
-[chuckles]

25:59.225 --> 26:00.226
You came for this?

26:00.893 --> 26:02.353
-Yes.
-Let's go.

26:02.436 --> 26:04.647
[inhales deeply] Will I do a good job?

26:05.648 --> 26:08.025
You've lectured
bigger audiences than this.

26:08.109 --> 26:10.569
Ugh, I'm so nervous though.

26:11.570 --> 26:12.780
[groans]

26:12.863 --> 26:14.073
Wish me luck!

26:16.784 --> 26:18.286
Says someone who'll do well.

26:18.369 --> 26:20.746
But I've never done it
at a place like this.

26:20.830 --> 26:22.832
[chattering, chuckling]

26:24.625 --> 26:26.127
-You're cheating!
-[Jenny] I got you!

26:27.753 --> 26:28.921
Eui-ju.

26:29.005 --> 26:30.506
What did she say?

26:31.257 --> 26:33.301
-We made up.
-You did?

26:33.968 --> 26:34.969
Yeah, we did.

26:35.052 --> 26:37.221
[applauding, cheering]

26:37.972 --> 26:41.142
IN MY OWN WAY,
AT A PACE THAT SUITS ME

26:43.227 --> 26:45.855
Hello, it's nice to meet you all.
My name is Na Deul-i.

26:45.938 --> 26:47.189
[funky, upbeat music playing]

26:47.273 --> 26:49.317
I've prepared a few slides about myself.

26:49.400 --> 26:50.776
Now, guess what this is.

26:50.860 --> 26:53.362
It's my very first test result
when I was in first grade.

26:54.322 --> 26:55.448
Strange, right?

26:55.531 --> 26:57.533
-Because I'm supposed to be a genius.
-[crowd chuckles]

26:57.616 --> 26:59.452
What's your standard in choosing a job?

26:59.535 --> 27:02.079
-[students] Fame. Money.
-Fame. Money. Right, money.

27:02.163 --> 27:05.708
They say science students score higher
on the MBTI Thinking scale.

27:05.791 --> 27:08.711
The real question most of you
are probably asking right now though is,

27:08.794 --> 27:10.713
"Are you seriously a T right now?"

27:10.796 --> 27:12.006
Yes, you should give it a try too.

27:12.089 --> 27:14.675
At that time, everyone was pretty sure

27:14.759 --> 27:16.761
that the Korean team
was going to place first,

27:16.844 --> 27:20.389
but someone decided to drop out
right at the end,

27:20.473 --> 27:22.183
and the team ended up placing second.

27:22.266 --> 27:23.517
Guess who that was.

27:26.187 --> 27:29.857
It was your math teacher right there,
Mr. Ga Woo-su.

27:29.940 --> 27:31.817
[crowd chuckling]

27:34.820 --> 27:38.783
I believe that all of you will be able to
find your own answer one day.

27:39.575 --> 27:40.910
It's so annoying

27:41.744 --> 27:43.120
that she's so cool.

27:43.746 --> 27:46.248
-[sighs]
-[Deul-i] I'll be rooting for you.

27:46.332 --> 27:49.960
All right. This was Na Deul-i.
Thank you for listening. Thank you.

27:58.469 --> 28:00.596
One, two, three.

28:01.889 --> 28:03.140
Go back inside now.

28:03.224 --> 28:06.685
[students] Thank you.

28:06.769 --> 28:08.020
Could you take a picture of us?

28:08.104 --> 28:10.064
-Mr. Ga, me too.
-Me too!

28:10.147 --> 28:11.273
Take one of us too!

28:12.608 --> 28:14.276
All right. One, two, three.

28:14.360 --> 28:15.653
[camera shutters]

28:16.237 --> 28:17.696
-Thank you.
-Mr. Ga, me too.

28:18.572 --> 28:19.573
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

28:19.657 --> 28:21.242
-One by one, yeah?
-[students] Yes!

28:21.325 --> 28:22.493
Oh, thank you. [chuckles]

28:24.495 --> 28:25.579
-One, two, three.
-[camera shutters]

28:25.663 --> 28:27.456
[students chuckle]

28:27.540 --> 28:29.291
-One, two, three.
-[camera shutters]

28:29.375 --> 28:30.626
-You're so cool.
-Thank you.

28:30.709 --> 28:32.670
Thank you. Thank you, thank you.

28:37.425 --> 28:38.426
Come. Come.

28:38.509 --> 28:40.177
[chuckles]

28:40.261 --> 28:41.679
All right. One, two, three.

28:41.762 --> 28:43.180
[camera shutters]

28:44.390 --> 28:45.391
[both] Thank you.

28:46.058 --> 28:49.019
I got to relax and pull it off
all thanks to you.

28:49.103 --> 28:50.521
-I really appreciate it.
-[chuckles]

28:51.730 --> 28:53.649
I was able to relax thanks to her.

28:56.861 --> 28:58.904
The after-school class
will have a pop quiz today.

28:58.988 --> 29:00.239
Write it on the blackboard.

29:00.322 --> 29:01.949
-Yes, sir.
-Go on.

29:02.616 --> 29:03.951
-Goodbye.
-Bye-bye now.

29:05.119 --> 29:07.705
-Let's go.
-[students chuckling]

29:07.788 --> 29:09.081
-Did you take it?
-Yeah.

29:09.165 --> 29:10.499
[chuckles]

29:12.960 --> 29:16.130
Whoa, they do make a great couple.

29:19.967 --> 29:21.010
Sorry.

29:24.096 --> 29:25.222
[sighs]

29:25.306 --> 29:26.557
Yeah, I know.

29:27.266 --> 29:29.268
He belongs with her and not me.

29:33.731 --> 29:34.732
Let's go.

29:36.817 --> 29:39.320
Happy you stayed for the research
instead of going to the States?

29:39.403 --> 29:43.532
CHAPTER 49:
THE ABSOLUT VALUE OF ROMANCE

29:43.616 --> 29:45.576
So, does that mean we're rivals now?

29:46.827 --> 29:48.037
Who will be first?

29:48.662 --> 29:51.040
I mean, who will find the proper answer.

29:52.833 --> 29:55.461
Yeah, I guess time will tell

29:56.212 --> 29:58.547
if math on its own has any value at all.

29:59.048 --> 30:00.341
[scoffs]

30:00.424 --> 30:02.009
You'll regret it when it's too late.

30:05.012 --> 30:06.305
Go on.

30:06.889 --> 30:09.433
[smacks lips] All right fine.
I'm leaving, okay? [scoffs]

30:10.476 --> 30:12.061
-Bye.
-Bye!

30:13.395 --> 30:15.856
VISITOR PARKING LOT

30:28.869 --> 30:30.955
[class] Hello, Mr. Ga.

30:31.038 --> 30:32.581
All right, there's a pop quiz today.

30:32.665 --> 30:34.500
You have 20 minutes
to solve the questions.

30:34.583 --> 30:35.584
Pass these back.

30:53.269 --> 30:54.728
PAST MATH EXAM QUESTIONS

30:55.854 --> 30:59.441
[pensive music playing]

31:01.193 --> 31:02.319
3. PROPERTIES
OF LOGARITHMIC FUNCTIONS

31:02.403 --> 31:03.404
2. MEAN VALUE THEOREM

31:03.487 --> 31:04.738
1. DIFFERENTIATION
OF POLYNOMIAL FUNCTION

31:13.247 --> 31:14.248
[exhales shakily]

31:19.628 --> 31:20.629
[sniffs]

31:30.889 --> 31:32.808
If you're done,
submit it and you can leave.

32:06.175 --> 32:07.217
Stop and bring it over.

32:11.930 --> 32:12.931
Bring it over.

32:36.538 --> 32:37.623
Leave it here and go home.

33:03.691 --> 33:06.568
[hopeful music playing]

33:20.207 --> 33:24.253
[Eui-ju] Absolute value refers
to something that exists solely as itself

33:24.336 --> 33:26.922
without being compared to
any other object.

33:27.464 --> 33:30.259
A state where no conditions
or constraints are attached

33:30.342 --> 33:32.010
and nothing can stand against it.

33:32.094 --> 33:34.972
Find the absolut value
of the following romance.

33:38.976 --> 33:42.438
What is the absolut value of
glasses divided by pigeon

33:42.521 --> 33:45.023
multiplied by the square root
of emergency room

33:45.107 --> 33:48.193
plus the square
of after-school class plus novel

33:48.277 --> 33:50.195
multiplied by the limit of bus stop?

34:18.891 --> 34:22.269
ABSOLUTE
ABSOLUTE

34:23.061 --> 34:24.813
-Seriously?
-Can't you even spell it right?

34:26.899 --> 34:28.358
I know how to spell it.

34:29.318 --> 34:30.486
This is just

34:31.069 --> 34:35.699
a literary device I used
to emphasize the word "absolute."

34:37.034 --> 34:38.160
[sighs]

34:38.243 --> 34:40.913
Both your spelling
and your equation are a mess.

34:41.830 --> 34:43.248
Is there an answer?

34:43.332 --> 34:46.043
Of course! This is the only problem
I've been working on lately.

34:46.752 --> 34:48.170
What's the answer then?

34:49.838 --> 34:50.839
I've got…

34:52.174 --> 34:53.509
only one answer.

34:54.676 --> 34:55.677
[sighs]

34:57.930 --> 34:59.014
To me…

35:04.978 --> 35:05.979
To me,

35:06.980 --> 35:08.023
the answer is…

35:15.864 --> 35:17.491
This absolut value…

35:21.620 --> 35:23.080
The value is you.

35:24.623 --> 35:26.542
[tender music playing]

35:28.293 --> 35:30.295
My absolut value of romance…

35:32.089 --> 35:33.674
is you, Mr. Ga.
